ssue bank and atlas of human treg gene expression to identify pathways in tissue immune regulation; the Treg Atlas, which recreates tissue states in tregs and reprograms blood-derived Tregs to recreate human tissue-specific pathways in vitro for target validation; and the Phenotypic Assay Cascade, a suite of high-throughput functional fingerprinting assays that test targets across donors and inflammatory contexts. The company develops TRB-061 an investigational tumor necrosis factor receptor 2 (TNFR2) agonist and fragment crystallizable-fusion (Fc-fusion) protein designed to selectively agonize TNFR2 to activate and expand Tregs in inflamed tissues. The company also develops TRB-071, an agonist designed to augment tissue Tregs and block an inflammatory signaling pathway, for inflammatory bowel disease. Additionally, it advances TRB-051, a partnered modulator of immune effector cells, for autoimmune and inflammatory diseases including lupus with cutaneous involvement. The company also advances preclinical-stage programs addressing tissue Treg biology informed by the Deep Biology Platform. TRex Bio, Inc. was incorporated in 2018 and is based in South San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Marion Johnston Erwin Jr. | Chairman & CEO | Age 64 | Compensation: $908,956 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 60 people. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture.","financial_summary":["TRex Bio, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $375M market cap on $0 of annual revenue.","The company is burning through $41M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +9.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","Net dilution runs at 11.2% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 42% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because i